ect suffix הִנְחַ֫נִי Gen 24:48 ; 2 masculine singular suffix הִנְחִתָם Neh 9:12 ; Imperfect suffix יַנְחֵ֫נִי Num 23:7 ; Psa 23:3 ; יַנְחֶ֫נּוּ Deut 32:12 ; Prov 18:16 ; 3 feminine singular תַּנְחֶה 6:22 , etc.; Infinitive construct suffix לְהַנְחֹתָּם Neh 9:19 ; לַנְחֹתָם Exod 13:21 ; &#8212; lead, guide (= Qal) followed by accusative of person Num 23:7 (J E; + מִן ). — 1Sam 22:4 (+ אֶתמְּֿנֵי ), 1Kin 10:26 ; 2Kin 18:11 see below נוח Hiph`il B. — of guiding= treating kindly (the helpless) Job 31:18 , of guiding constellations 38:32 (|| הוציא ); usually subject ׳י Gen 24:48 (J; followed by בַּדֶּרֶךְ ) Deut 32:12 ; Psa 78:14 . 78:53 . 78:72 (Israel as flock; || רעה ); Isa 57:18 ; Psa 107:30 (followed by אֶלֿ ); compare of pillar of cloud Exod 13:21 (J), Neh 9:12 , 19 ; also Job 12:23 **read properly וַיַּנִּחֵ֥֥ and leaves them ( Jer 14:9 ) (|| שׁטח ), Psa 67:5 ; especially in path of blessing 23:3 ; 31:4 (|| נהל ), 61:3 (followed by בְּ ), 73:24 ; compare 43:3 ; 139:10 (|| אחז ), 143:10 (followed by בְּ ); also of instruction, etc., Prov 6:22 ; 11:3 ; 18:16 (followed by לִפְנֵי ). I. נחל (√ of following; compare Arabic give for one's own, bestow , so Sabean נחל SabDenkm No. 9. i. 10; No. 15, i. 4; compare pp. 41, 65 ; hence נַחֲלָה originally gift , as Sabean נחלת Levy-Os ZMG xix (1865), 284 SabDenkm l.c. ; Minaean id. , Hom Südar. Chrest. 128 ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 10 26","keyReferences":["1Kgs 10 26","1Sam 22 4","2Kgs 18 11","Deut 32 12","Exod 13 17","Exod 13 21","Exod 15 13","Exod 32 34"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":39,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 10 26","book":"1Kgs","chapter":10,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּנְחֵ/ם֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3ms/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 22 4","book":"1Sam","chapter":22,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּנְחֵ֕/ם","sou